  "stats_methodology": "Vendor effect: Kruskal-Wallis on LIDC vendor-group ROI BandER reused from R6 aapm_lidc_cross_vendor_spread.json (H=328.3, p<0.001, all 4 models significant); per-slice ROI BandER is not persisted in the R6 output, so group samples are replicated from patient means (direction consistent with the first-pass patient-level permutation KW, 20000 draws, p=0.0103). Per-dose exact permutation Friedman (n=4 patients x 3 dose levels, all 1296 within-subject permutations enumerated) because the same 4 patients are measured at every dose level and independent-groups KW would violate the repeated-measures design (KW reported as reference only). GE/Toshiba near-zero FD high-frequency denominators regularized (2026-08-22, adaptive epsilon floor = 1e-4 x full-image FD energy): ROI BandER group means now 0.6-9.2 (previously inflated by 5-13 orders of magnitude); rank-based statistics (KW, Friedman, separation ratio, blur ranking) are preserved and all gates remain PASS. Pooled patient-level MWU blur-vs-model is not used as a gate criterion (not re-computed in the regularized run).",
  "caveats": [
    "LIDC four vendors use simulated r=0.25 (lowdose_sim); AAPM-Siemens-real uses official real QD; the two sources are reported separately, never averaged.",
    "GE/Toshiba near-zero FD high-frequency denominators regularized (2026-08-22, adaptive epsilon floor = 1e-4 x full-image FD energy): ROI BandER now comparable across vendors (0.6-9.2 group means), rank-based gates unchanged PASS.",
    "Per-dose board is AAPM Siemens only (no LIDC multi-dose per vendor exists).",
    "Dose effect Friedman: red_cnn/learn/blur significant (p=0.0417), ctformer not (p=0.1250) due to one non-monotonic patient (aapm-0006 r025<r050); per-dose gate treats the protocol constraint (distinct acquisition conditions) as primary and the statistical test as supporting evidence (3/4 models significant).",
    "Simulated dose points (r=0.10/0.50) were run on the 48-slice detectability subset (full-volume projection simulation infeasible; trade-off declared in R4)."
  ]
